WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.890
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.537
which takes about fifty-five
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.788
You'll explain the documented lockout,

4
00:00:07.788 --> 00:00:11.937
and why the emergency accounts come
before any approval is switched on.

5
00:00:11.937 --> 00:00:16.089
You'll name what Microsoft Learn's
standard asks of each emergency account,

6
00:00:16.089 --> 00:00:17.963
and the rule that checks each item.

7
00:00:17.963 --> 00:00:21.533
You'll explain why the
alert reads three tables,

8
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:25.012
not one, and why it matches
object I D's, not names.

9
00:00:25.012 --> 00:00:27.462
You'll run the check
and read its findings.

10
00:00:27.462 --> 00:00:31.276
And you'll say why every enforced
Conditional Access policy

11
00:00:31.276 --> 00:00:34.937
must exclude the accounts, and
why a report-only one needn't.

12
00:00:34.937 --> 00:00:37.213
Before you start, finish Module 1:

13
00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:41.088
this lab uses its module and
its fictional tenant again.

14
00:00:41.088 --> 00:00:44.662
Reading K Q L helps for the
alert, but isn't required.

15
00:00:44.662 --> 00:00:47.564
Lab 2 needs a worldwide
or G C C test tenant

16
00:00:47.564 --> 00:00:51.120
with a test Azure
subscription, never production.
